---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import ToolReview from '../../components/ToolReview.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const leaving = appBySlug('brevo')!;
const path = '/alternatives/brevo-alternative';
const title = 'Best Brevo Alternatives for Shopify (2026)';
const desc = 'Compare Brevo with eight Shopify alternatives by required workflows, current plan conditions, ownership and migration readiness.';

const altSlugs = ['sequenzy', 'omnisend', 'klaviyo', 'drip', 'mailchimp', 'shopify-email', 'tinyemail', 'activecampaign'];
const alternatives = altSlugs.map((s) => appBySlug(s)!);

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Why evaluate a Brevo replacement?",
    "answer": "Evaluate a demonstrated workflow, cost or staffing mismatch. Test the current Brevo PushOwl integration before attributing a gap to Brevo as a whole."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which alternative is best?",
    "answer": "There is no universal winner. Have the intended operator test required journeys and compare matched costs; the options below are candidates, not performance rankings."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can Brevo keep transactional email?",
    "answer": "A split can work if each purpose has one sender and queue owner. Verify templates, credentials, permission boundaries and suppression; separate domains alone do not prevent duplicate sends or establish permission."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is Mailchimp worth considering?",
    "answer": "Yes, when its proposed campaign workflow, integration and operator fit meet the requirements. Familiarity can reduce training work, but does not prove savings or equivalent automation."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does migration transfer workflows?",
    "answer": "Do not assume it does. Verify available exports, stable identity mapping and destination event coverage, then rebuild and test conditions, delays, purchase exits and queue cancellation."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I compare pricing?",
    "answer": "Use the single matched cost method below. Brevo email volume also determines contact storage limits; a large stored list with few sends is not automatically an unlimited-contact bargain."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I move SMS too?",
    "answer": "Check destination country support, sender registration, approvals, number portability and current channel permission before moving any traffic. An email integration does not establish SMS eligibility."
  },
  {
    "question": "When should I stay?",
    "answer": "Stay when the actual plan, integration and named operators meet required journeys and costs. Newsletter simplicity or CRM needs can justify retention; neither implies that future replenishment needs are already solved."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-14">
    <nav><a class="link" href="/alternatives">Alternatives</a> / Brevo alternatives</nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl">
      <p class="catalog-kicker">Commerce, CRM and transactional ownership</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Brevo alternatives for Shopify</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 text-xl">Choose whether to retain, split or replace Brevo from a demonstrated gap. A replacement may suit a store’s catalog journeys or operating team better, but switching does not itself improve retention. Keep useful newsletters, sales workflows and transactional services in the decision.</p>
    </header>
    <TldrBox title="Options by required job" picks={[
      { label: 'Assisted workflow drafting', tool: 'Sequenzy', reason: 'Test operator control and event coverage.' },
      { label: 'Commerce campaign workflow', tool: 'Omnisend', reason: 'Reproduce cart and launch requirements.' },
      { label: 'Catalog segmentation', tool: 'Klaviyo', reason: 'Test required fields and event availability.' },
      { label: 'Visual branching', tool: 'Drip', reason: 'Have the intended owner maintain a sample journey.' },
      { label: 'Campaign operations', tool: 'Mailchimp', reason: 'Compare the actual integration and team workflow.' },
    ]} />
    <article class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl py-10">
      <h2>Establish the current Brevo baseline</h2>
      <p>Brevo documents a <a class="link" href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360014912879">Brevo PushOwl Shopify app</a>. Identify the installed integration and account arrangement, then verify current customer, product and event mappings. Do not judge the current service from an older connector or assume every variant field and event is available.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/208589409">Brevo plan documentation</a> ties the selected email volume to pricing and contact storage limits. Check the required automation, reporting, users and CRM entitlements under the offered plan and add-ons. Low send frequency does not remove storage limits. CRM breadth may be useful for wholesale follow-up even when marketing needs a different operator.</p>
      <p>For SMS, check <a class="link" href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/208717449">supported destinations and destination-based credits</a>, and <a class="link" href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/28255350696466">sender registration requirements</a>. Confirm regional sender approvals, allowed content, sending times and account eligibility. Email permission is not SMS permission; no migration date can be promised before these dependencies pass.</p>
      <h2>Proposed merchant tests, not performed results</h2>
      <p><strong>Specialty tea and artisan coffee:</strong> test blend and pack-size mapping, subscription versus one-off orders, gifts and repeat purchases. Derive replenishment timing from product use and observed eligible repeat orders; a fixed thirty-day cycle is not evidence. A French tea shop could retain Brevo transactional sending while testing another marketing tool, subject to ownership controls below.</p>
      <p><strong>Vinyl shop:</strong> test VIP drop announcements, pressing restocks and sold-out exits before a release. <strong>Poster print shop:</strong> model a proposed 22,000 stored contacts and 8,000 monthly email sends against current storage and send tiers; this is a quote fixture, not a merchant saving or a twelve-percent revenue opportunity.</p>
      <p><strong>Mechanical keyboards:</strong> preserve switch preferences and variant IDs, including missing or conflicting values. <strong>Climbing and camping gear:</strong> test collection and variant metafields without treating a browse event as marketing permission. <strong>Board games:</strong> replay a purchase event and confirm a pending recovery message is cancelled rather than duplicated.</p>
      <p><strong>Pottery studio:</strong> distinguish class leads, wholesale quotes and mug customers. Wholesale climbing dealers and coffee cupping invitees need their own purpose and eligibility rules; a sales deal or inquiry must not automatically enroll someone in DTC promotions. Keep useful CRM fields and document any lossy mappings.</p>
      <h2>One matched cost method</h2>
      <p><strong>Cost comparison:</strong> For the same month, currency, tax treatment, eligible audience, stored contacts, billable profiles, email sends, destination-specific SMS segments and required features, obtain current quotes. Add platform and usage fees, integrations, CRM seats, services and monthly staff hours multiplied by the same hourly rate. Show one-time setup and overlap costs separately; do not compare them with a recurring monthly fee as if their units matched. Record billing cadence, allowances and overages. The poster-shop fixture supplies only contacts and sends, so it cannot establish an equivalent price.</p>
      <p>Compare attributed order revenue using the same event definition and attribution window. Estimate incremental contribution separately with eligible randomized cohorts where feasible, accounting for discounts, returns, product margin and messaging costs. Choose duration and sample size from volume and the question; report uncertainty. Neither abandoned checkout value nor a dashboard attribution total proves recoverable profit.</p>
    </article>
    <section class="space-y-10 pb-12">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-black">Eight options to evaluate</h2>
      <p>Order is for navigation. Shared catalog cards below include editorial descriptors, strengths, limitations and feature labels; they are not verified plan entitlements or proof of superiority. Confirm each requirement with the provider and a store-specific test. No feature parity, migration duration or merchant outcome is established here.</p>
      <ToolReview app={alternatives[0]} rank={1} paragraphs={["Sequenzy publishes email-volume pricing and advertises Shopify integration. Evaluate assisted drafting and lifecycle operation with the tea replenishment fixture; do not infer unlimited storage or stronger retention from the billing basis.", "Have the operator verify event mappings, suppression and maintainable branching. Software still needs an accountable owner."]} />
      <ToolReview app={alternatives[1]} rank={2} paragraphs={["Evaluate Omnisend for the vinyl release, welcome and cart jobs. Test inventory exits, actual channel availability and the proposed plan before judging setup effort.", "Compare <a class=\"link\" href=\"/compare/brevo-vs-omnisend\">Brevo vs Omnisend</a> using the same requirements; prebuilt templates do not establish launch speed."]} />
      <ToolReview app={alternatives[2]} rank={3} paragraphs={["Evaluate Klaviyo for climbing-gear collection and keyboard variant segmentation. Verify the fields and event history actually available to the intended account.", "Assign a segment owner and compare billable profiles, sends and required features rather than assuming a universal data advantage."]} />
      <ToolReview app={alternatives[3]} rank={4} paragraphs={["Evaluate Drip for board-game branching when the operator prefers a visual workflow. Test duplicate purchases, missing fields and maintenance effort.", "Confirm current Shopify event coverage and plan limits before transferring any queue."]} />
      <ToolReview app={alternatives[4]} rank={5} paragraphs={["Evaluate Mailchimp for campaign approvals and a team familiar with its workflow. Reproduce the required Shopify customer journeys before deciding fit.", "A generalist can be appropriate; familiarity does not establish feature parity, savings or future regret."]} />
      <ToolReview app={alternatives[5]} rank={6} paragraphs={["Evaluate Shopify Email / Shopify Messaging when operating campaigns within Shopify admin fits the team. Test required templates and any Flow dependencies.", "Confirm current naming, account availability, triggers and channel entitlements with Shopify before planning cutover."]} />
      <ToolReview app={alternatives[6]} rank={7} paragraphs={["Evaluate tinyEmail for a deliberately focused newsletter workflow. Test audience updates, campaign approvals and the required automation rather than assuming inadequacy from store size.", "Confirm current integrations and operator workload; no order-count threshold determines fit."]} />
      <ToolReview app={alternatives[7]} rank={8} paragraphs={["Evaluate ActiveCampaign when pottery wholesale follow-up and DTC journeys need coordinated ownership. Test deal-state exits alongside purchases and permission.", "Check required CRM entitlements, users and commerce mappings; sharing a database does not resolve purpose boundaries."]} />
    </section>
    <article class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl pb-12">
      <h2>Cut over by readiness</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Inventory forms, Privy and Justuno routes, integrations, credentials, sending domains, templates and every live delay or queue. Preserve source IDs, field meanings, export limits and required records; do not equate engagement with permission.</li>
        <li>Record permission authority by channel and purpose, signup source, disclosure version, timestamps, withdrawals and suppressions. Resolve guest and account identities using stable Shopify customer and order IDs; quarantine ambiguous merges rather than treating email equality as identity proof.</li>
        <li>Specify triggers, delays and purchase, subscription, stock and CRM deal exits. Test gift orders, refunds, duplicate and late events, current opt-outs and missing attributes. Recheck eligibility immediately before dispatch, including new purchases that invalidate cart or replenishment reminders.</li>
        <li>Assign one sender and queue owner per journey. Cancel or drain old queued messages and disable old triggers before activating replacements. Reconcile popup destinations and webhooks. Preserve a dispatch ledger keyed by event, identity, purpose and journey to deduplicate replayed events across systems.</li>
        <li>Keep transactional and marketing purposes explicit. Audit Shopify notifications, Brevo SMTP/API and destination sends so order confirmations have one owner. Authenticate domains and review delivery; separate subdomains neither guarantee reputation isolation nor authorize promotional content in service messages.</li>
        <li>Test rollback before launch: pause replacement dispatch, cancel its queued work, reconcile purchases, suppressions and the dispatch ledger, then re-enable only eligible unsent work in the prior system. Never blindly replay the export or run both queues.</li>
        <li>Hand over the event map, credentials access, queue controls, reconciliation alerts and reporting definitions to named marketing, sales, technical and finance owners. Require the backup operator to demonstrate stopping a journey and resolving a failed sync. Cancel contracts or remove credentials only after retained dependencies and record obligations pass.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Advance after these gates pass, rather than on a four-week or ninety-day calendar. A valid decision may be to stay, repair the current integration, split purposes or migrate selected journeys. None guarantees continuity of attribution or performance.</p>
      <h2>Sources and related reading</h2>
      <p>Primary documentation checked 25 November 2026. <a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/pricing">Sequenzy pricing</a> supports its advertised pricing basis, not the proposed merchant outcomes. Recheck all quotes and entitlements before purchase.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="/apps/brevo">Brevo review</a> · <a class="link" href="/compare/brevo-vs-omnisend">Brevo vs Omnisend</a> · <a class="link" href="/compare/brevo-vs-mailchimp">Brevo vs Mailchimp</a> · <a class="link" href="/alternatives">All alternatives</a></p>
    </article>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Brevo alternatives FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
